## THE 12 CHANGES — every one is mandatory

### 1. KILLER-LEVEL ANIMATIONS (priority #1 — make them DIFFERENT, not the same springs)
Build #4 failed here because prompt v2 specified springs, not visible signatures, and there were no acceptance criteria. This time every transition has a VISIBLE signature + a screen-recorded acceptance test (point 12 + brief §2.5).
- Use the stable M3 Expressive APIs — `MotionScheme.expressive()` + `MaterialExpressiveTheme` from `androidx.compose.material3` **1.5.0** (BOM 2026.11.01) — wherever they fit, instead of hand-tuned constants. Token table below is the fallback/verification target.
- Island expand idle→medium: duration 0.35 s, bounce 0.15 (≈ response 0.35, damping 0.85). Island expand medium→full: duration 0.42 s, bounce 0.18 (Apple sheet-present). Island collapse: duration 0.32 s, bounce 0.
- Island morph (width/height/corner radius): M3 Expressive spatial default — damping 0.8, stiffness 380 (settles 460 ms, 1.5% overshoot). Alert arrival playful pop: M3 Expressive spatial fast — damping 0.6, stiffness 800 (380 ms, 9.5% overshoot). Colour/opacity fades: M3 Expressive effects default — damping 1.0, stiffness 1600 (260 ms, 0 overshoot); fast 3800 (170 ms).
- Button press: scale 0.97, spring 0.16 s bounce 0; release 0.3 s bounce 0.25. Hero/expressive actions may scale to 1.15. Press radius-squish: corner radius rounds more on press, springs back on release (M3E).
- Content crossfade inside the island: 200 ms, emphasized-decelerate cubic-bezier(0.05, 0.7, 0.1, 1). Stagger arrivals by 45 ms.
- HOW IT ACTUALLY COMES IN (observed in real apps — copy the behaviour, not the code): nothing slides or fades in from off-screen (iOS). The black pill already sitting on the camera *stretches* — first wider, then taller, corners blooming from ~18 dp to 36 dp radius — the leading icon pinned in place and travelling with the shape, content fading in only once the box is mostly grown. Content holds at 0% opacity for the first ~30% of the expand (~120–150 ms), then fades + rises 8 dp over ~200 ms. A notification does the same unprompted, briefly, then melts back to the pill. Expand has a 2–4% width overshoot ("squish") that settles; collapse has ZERO overshoot (critically damped, damping 1.0, ~300–350 ms). Interrupt mid-flight (tap Medium then immediately Full): the spring retargets with live velocity — never restart from zero, never snap.
- LIQUID EXPANSION (from Akira9021): when the island expands, the content grows TOGETHER with the island and emerges from a blur — never a hard pop. When it collapses, content shrinks back into the camera hole.
- DROPLET SPLIT: when a second activity starts while one is showing, it splits off the pill like a droplet into a small bubble beside the island, with a +1 badge; tap the bubble to switch. (ajitpal model: one in island, next in a circle beside it with +1 badge, tap to switch, long-press to see all.)
- FINGER-FOLLOWING PULL-DOWN: pulling down on the pill expands it following the finger; push left/right on the collapsed pill = next/previous track.
- ANIMATION STYLE PICKER in Settings → Motion: three named styles — "Springy" (playful overshoot, bouncy), "Standard" (balanced spring), "Calm" (minimal bounce, fastest settle) — plus elasticity and duration sliders. Motion rule (from Dynamic Ledge v1.5.0): the island springs open with a little overshoot and settles back WITHOUT a bounce; collapse never bounces. Springy vs Calm must be MEASURABLY different (Springy visibly overshoots, Calm settles with no overshoot) — verify from a screen recording.
- OPENING vs CONTENT EFFECTS (from Material Capsule v19.4): the style picker sets TWO things separately — the capsule OPENING effect (how the pill grows: liquid, spring, smooth, pop) and the CONTENT effect (how text/icons arrive inside it: fade, slide-up, scale-in, blur-in). Settings → Motion is split into two screens: "Background" (pill colour/glass/density) and "Animations" (opening effect, content effect, elasticity, duration). Both must visibly change the feel.
- In-pill swipes on the collapsed pill: swipe left/right = next/prev track (music) or cycle notifications; swipe on the pill adjusts media volume (dynamicBar idea).
- EXPANDED-CARD SWIPES (from dynamicSpot v3.x): in an expanded notification card, swipe right = next notification, swipe left = dismiss/clear it. Both directions and long-press are configurable in Settings → Motion → Gestures.
- TRANSIENT vs PERSISTENT: status events (charging, battery, Bluetooth, unlock) show as a Mini Capsule that auto-dismisses after 2–4 seconds. Ongoing activities (music, timer) stay as a persistent docked card. The island is QUIET by default — it only appears when it has something to say. Mini Capsules are customisable (Settings → Motion → Mini Capsules): size, auto-dismiss time (2–4 s default), and which events use them.
- Music visualizer bars: animate scaleY only, ~10–14 Hz visual update, eased, never layout; pause bars when paused; 3–5 bars.
- Timer tick: text change only, tabular numerals, 150 ms crossfade; the container NEVER re-animates each second.
- Morph between tabs/states: same container, same spring; outgoing content fades out in the first 150 ms, incoming fades in after; the icon travels, never cross-fades a duplicate.

### 2. NOTHING EVER GOES INTO THE CAMERA (MUST-FIX — this bug survived build #3 AND build #4)
- ROOT CAUSE (do not repeat it): build #4's compact pill was a wrap-content `Row` centered on the screen whose "camera clearance" was just a fixed `Spacer` between the left and right slots. The spacer sits over the hole ONLY if the two slots are exactly equal width — and they never are. Every state has a narrow left slot (one icon) and a wide right slot (text), so the text drifts left by `(rightSlot − leftSlot) / 2`, straight under the punch-hole. Measured penetration in build #4: notification 25.5 dp, alert 26.5 dp, music 28 dp, charging 22.5 dp, timer 8.5 dp. The build-#4 checklist claimed "Strict >= 8dp cutout clearance" but never cited `CompactPillView` — it checked the mechanism, not the invariant. There was NO dead-zone test anywhere.
- HARD RULE, enforced in code: no text, icon, artwork, badge, or progress pixel within 8 dp of the punch-hole edge in ANY state (idle, compact, medium, split, expanded, calibration preview, transient banner).
- **Exclusion zone = the FULL detected cutout rect, expanded by 8 dp on all sides. Never hardcode 26 dp (or any dp value).** Compute it at runtime from `DisplayCutout.getBoundingRects()` / `getSafeInsetTop()`. On Alex's phone the detected cutout is 74×93 px ≈ 26×33 dp — build #4's clearance height was 26 dp, **7 dp SHORTER than the real 33 dp cutout**. That is very likely why text still goes under the camera. At his measured cutout the exclusion must be ≥42 dp wide × 49 dp tall (33 + 8 + 8). Re-measure on every launch, on rotation, and on configuration change. If `DisplayCutout` is null, fall back to status-bar height + 8 dp. Every pill/alert layout must query the live rect at draw time, not a cached constant.
- **Compact pill fix (Option A, required): fixed equal-width slots.** Replace the pill Row with two fixed-width slots: **left 88 dp, right 88 dp**, content centered in its slot; spacer between them = `holeW + 16 dp` (42 dp at defaults); 10 dp outer padding. Pill total = 238 dp at defaults. Equal slots make the drift term `(L−R)/2` = 0 for every state, every text length. Touch window must follow: `IslandService.kt:511` hardcodes COMPACT touch width 228 dp — smaller than the 238 dp pill. Change to `pillWidthDp + 16 dp`, recomputed on every mode/size change. Never a hardcoded touch width again.
- Slot content caps (hard `widthIn(max=…)` + `maxLines=1` + `TextOverflow.Ellipsis`, inside the 88 dp slot): music title ≤ **66 dp** (66 + 6 gap + 16 waveform = 88); notification/alert text ≤ **80 dp**; timer digits no cap needed ("23:59:59" ≈ 58 dp) but must stay inside the slot; charging: bar 26 + 5 + text ≤ 57 dp — if it overflows, drop the wattage first, then show `%` only; left slot: icon/artwork only (22 dp max), centered, no text. 2 dp safety inset: right-slot text starts 2 dp inside the slot edge (effective clearance 10 dp).
- **Notification pill rules:** compact pill shows **app icon (left) + app name only (right)** — never the notification `title`, never the `text`/body, never a full sentence. (The "Saved to Photo..." text was a verbatim notification title from the notifying app, read with no truncation.) Title/text live only in the expanded card and the inbox, below the camera band. App name: `widthIn(max=80 dp)`, `maxLines=1`, ellipsis. Blank app name → literal `"Notification"`.
- **Expanded / medium cards:** first content row below the header must start at **y ≥ holeBottom + 8 dp** (≥ 41 dp at measured cutout). Medium body today sits at exactly +8 dp — raise to **+12 dp** for margin. Header rows: replace or constrain the `SpaceBetween + fixed spacer` pattern — left group `widthIn(max=120 dp)` from the card's left inner edge, right group `widthIn(max=120 dp)` from the right inner edge, both with ellipsis. Header height stays `holeH + 16 dp` (≥ 42 dp). No tab content may be placed in the header band. Expanded card top margin: 8 dp from screen top; no text in the top 32 dp of the card.
- **SPLIT mode:** the companion bubble + pill layout must re-derive from the fixed-slot geometry — the old 22 dp pill shift that pushed notification text ~47 dp under the hole must not recur.
- **RED CALIBRATE MODE** (from ajitpal/Akira9021): in Settings → Pill → Calibrate, the island turns red and the user slides it until it exactly covers the camera hole, with X/Y/width/height sliders and a live preview. The island must grow OUT OF the camera and shrink back INTO it. **Gate:** until calibration is done (auto-detect run) or "use defaults" is explicitly confirmed, the island shows the idle ring only — no compact content. **Live preview must render the real `CompactPillView`** with worst-case fixtures: a 60-char notification title, a 30-char app name, a 60-char music title, charging 100% + 99W. Sliders show live dp values **and** draw the computed exclusion zone as a red dashed rect. Calibration screen must show: detected rect in px (74×93) and dp (26×33); safe insets in px/dp; computed exclusion rect in px and dp; a **live overlay** drawing the exclusion zone as a red dashed outline around the camera; a "Test alert" button firing a long-name alert pill. Auto-detect writes the measured rect into settings **and** forces a re-preview + explicit user confirm ("text clears the camera").
- **LANDSCAPE:** when the phone rotates, re-read `DisplayCutout.boundingRects`, recompute the hole center, and **move the island anchor to the hole's new position** — never leave it at the portrait top-center. Overlay window gravity/position and the touch window must follow in the same frame. In landscape the hole sits on the left/right edge, vertically centered: use a **vertical two-sided layout** (icon/state above the hole, value below it), same 8 dp rule on the vertical axis, same fixed-equal-slot rule. Verify on the "Try it" screen by rotating the phone. Current code has zero orientation handling — this is new code, not a tweak.
- **Runtime self-check (a test that fails the build):** add `CameraDeadZoneTest` to `app/src/test/` and to the FINISH gate (`gradle testDebugUnitTest` must pass before push): (a) geometry unit test — pure function `DeadZoneGeometry.isSafe(leftSlotDp, rightSlotDp, holeWidthDp)` asserting the spacer is centered (slots equal within 0.5 dp) and both slots' content starts outside the exclusion zone, tested at hole widths 14 dp and 80 dp; (b) Compose UI test (Robolectric) — render `CompactPillView`, `MediumPillView`, `ExpandedIslandCard` with worst-case fixtures (60-char notification title, 30-char app name, 60-char music title, 100% + 99W charging, 23:59:59 timer, 40-char alert, SPLIT with companion left and right) at hole widths 14/26/80 dp, assert via semantics/`LayoutCoordinates` that **no `Text` node's bounds intersect the exclusion rect** — fails the build on any intersection; (c) debug-only runtime guard — `onGloballyPositioned` pass over island `Text` nodes draws a red flashing border + logs if any text rect intersects the exclusion zone (debug-only, zero release cost). Tests must use LONG fixtures — the audit failure was short fixtures. Name fixtures after the real bug: `"Saved to Photos"`, 60-char music title, etc.
- Add a "Try it" demo screen (Settings → Motion → Try it): every island state (music, timer, charging, notification) playable on one screen with a live preview. Add a first-run Tips screen (Settings → About → Tips to reopen): one row per gesture with a live mini-demo — tap = medium, 2nd tap = full, long-press = full, swipe L/R = next/prev track, pull down = expand.
- **"WHEN IDLE" setting** (Settings → Pill): three choices — Camera Only (default, the locked thin-border idle), Info Pill, Hidden. Info Pill shows one user-chosen item on each side of the camera: Time, Battery (green bolt while charging, RED at 15% or less), Date, Next Alarm (within 24 h), Unread count, Network, Battery % or Net Speed, or Nothing. Long-press the info pill = tools; swipe down = inbox. Idle slots must use the same fixed-slot layout as above.

### 3. COMPACT EXPANSION (NEW — build #4's cap was the bug)
- Build #4's cap: 388 dp wide = 98.7% of the 393 dp screen (2.5 dp margins — effectively edge-to-edge), 216 dp tall = 24.8% of screen height. Apple caps expanded height at **160 pt**; 216 dp is 35% taller than Apple's maximum and 66% taller than Apple's typical media card (130 pt). No real island app expands that big. dynamicSpot's own users complain its popups got "way too big… tons of empty space" — do NOT repeat that.
- **There must be no single shared fixed box. Height is content-sized per tab, under a hard cap.** Apple's HIG rule: "Dynamically change the height… When there's less information to show, reduce the height to only use the space needed."
- **Size spec (dp; px = dp × 2.75):** idle pill 120 × 36 dp; compact (music/timer running) 200–230 × 37 dp; system glimpse (charging, silent — transient, never full) 200–260 dp wide, 48–64 dp tall, content-sized; **MEDIUM (1st tap): 320 dp wide (81.4%), content-sized, 96–120 dp max, radius 28 dp, 36 dp margins each side, top 8 dp; FULL (2nd tap): 360 dp wide (91.6%, HARD CAP, never exceed), content-sized, ABSOLUTE MAX 160 dp tall, radius 36 dp, 16 dp margins each side, top 8 dp.**
- **Max expanded height per tab (FULL; MEDIUM in brackets):** Music **132 dp** (108); Timer **124 dp** (96); Notification/Alerts **144 dp** (96, scrolls inside beyond 4 lines — never grows taller); Shelf **152 dp** (112, header + 3 items max, scroll inside beyond 3); Notes **148 dp** (108, 3 notes max visible, scroll inside); Tools/dock **160 dp ceiling, only this tab may reach it** (120); Calculator **160 dp ceiling** (120, compact 4-column keypad only, no history row in full); Search **160 dp ceiling** (112, field + 3 suggestions max). 160 dp = 18.3% of screen height. The card must never cover the top quarter of the screen.
- **1st tap → Medium** (320 dp, ≤120 dp, primary action only — must feel like the island grew, not like a panel opened). **2nd tap → Full** (360 dp, per-tab cap, secondary rows appear). Toggleable in Settings; if disabled, 1st tap goes straight to Full — still under the same 360×160 cap.
- **Collapse is staged:** Full → Medium → Compact/Idle, never Full → nothing in one jump (a jump reads as a crash). Swipe-down or Back steps down one tier at a time.
- **Width and height are independent caps:** a tab with little content is 320×96, not 320×120 with dead space. Empty space inside the card is the exact "too big" complaint.

### 4. UI — make it look like Apple, Meta and Google built it together (priority #3)
- **Glass — concrete spec, not "make it glassy":** primary in-app glass engine is **Haze 2.1.0 stable** (`hazeGlassContainer` merges island+dock+circle into one shape). `GlassStyle.clear` for the island pill and dock (edge-band refraction, background stays visible — the background must show clearly through it); `GlassStyle.regular` for the expanded deck where readability matters. Both draw 0.7 dp black outline at 40% opacity outside + 1 dp light band inside top/bottom edges. Parameters: rimHighlight (thin light band just inside top/bottom), shape (`RoundedCornerShape` or `ContinuousRoundedCornerShape`, smoothing 0–1), surfaceProfile (Circle / Squircle / Lip / Concave). **Kyant Backdrop 2.0.1 is fallback only** (AGSL refraction + blur + vibrancy ×1.5 + lens water-drop ring; effect primitives, not components — build your own). Do NOT use ahmedzer/LiquidGlass or BuildItCode/LiquidGlass (no license). The zerowing liquid/glass WEB library is WEB-ONLY — never for the Android overlay (it refracts only its own backdrop, never the live app behind it).
- **Cross-window blur for the overlay:** `FLAG_BLUR_BEHIND` + `blurBehindRadius` (AOSP guidance: 20 px depth-of-field / 80 px frosted glass, avoid >150 px) + low-alpha tint + bright specular top-edge rim + 1 px light border + inner shadow. That reads as real glass. Do NOT claim refraction displacement of the system-blurred backdrop — the app cannot sample that texture. Listen via `addCrossWindowBlurEnabledListener` / `isCrossWindowBlurEnabled` and fall back to a translucent scrim. **Whether MIUI 14 on the Redmi Note 10 Pro honors it is UNVERIFIED — phone-test it first with a minimal probe; if it fails, the fallback below must look finished, not broken.**
- **Liquid Glass as a Settings option (NEW):** Settings → Look → Pill style offers **Dark / Apple Glass / Liquid Glass — with a live preview per style. NOT forced on everyone.** Dark = pure opaque black pill, unchanged. Apple Glass = the existing glass pill (blur 20–24 px, saturate 150–180%, tint white 8–14% light / black 20–28% dark, 1 px specular top border). Liquid Glass = Kyant Backdrop 2.0.1 for **in-app screens** (Settings, Shelf, Setup Wizard, home hub — real AGSL refraction of the app's own content, API 33+ = this phone exactly) + cross-window blur + Haze `GlassStyle.clear` for the **floating overlay**. The picker screen shows a live mini-island in each of the three styles over a sample backdrop, updating in real time as the user taps each option. **Fallback (mandatory):** if MIUI cross-window blur fails on his phone, the **overlay falls back gracefully to the Apple-glass look** (translucent scrim + rim light + tint, no refraction claim), while **in-app screens keep real liquid glass**. No half-rendered refraction, no error state, no user-facing warning.
- **Glass density slider** in Settings → Look drags the glass from opaque to fully clear (the iOS 27 direction) — it must visibly change the pill and dock glass in real time, for all glass styles.
- **Glass guardrails (732G):** glass ONLY on the island and dock chrome (max ~5–10 surfaces); static wash elsewhere; NEVER glass on content cards, lists, or scrollable panels; NEVER glass-on-glass; never run a shader during island spring animations (those stay on `graphicsLayer`); DPR capped; `reduce-motion` respected; frosted fallback always in place. Prism lagged on this phone — same rules apply.
- Shape scale: pill = full; cards 28 dp; sheets 32 dp; chips 8 dp. Concentric corners (inner radius = outer radius − padding). Expanded corner radius 36 dp (full tier) / 28 dp (medium).
- Colour coding by activity — must be VISIBLE (build #4 hid it): timer = orange, charging/battery = green, music = album-art/waveform accent. Primary colour only on the most important action; container/on-container tone delta ≥ 40. **WAVY PROGRESS (M3E stable):** the music seek bar and the timer progress use the M3 Expressive wavy progress indicator (the wave, not a flat bar). **ROTATING ALBUM ART:** in the expanded music card, the album artwork slowly rotates while playing and stops when paused (toggleable in Settings → Look). Compact pill background may tint from the artwork colour.
- Material You: the glass pill tints from the wallpaper colour; the black pill stays pure opaque black. M3E colour: dynamic colour from wallpaper → tonal palettes; style with roles not hexes (`primaryContainer`, `surfaceContainerLow/High/Highest`, `outline`); build depth with the `surfaceContainer` ladder, not shadows. Typography: emphasized styles, heavier headlines; tabular numerals for timer.
- Expanded card anatomy (Apple's best cards + Dynamic Ledge Home): top row = icon + title + subtitle; middle = progress bar; bottom = control row (prev/pause/next, or pause/stop, or one action button). **EXPANDED HOME LAYOUT (Dynamic Ledge):** the expanded view is a Home — live activity FIRST (music/timer/notification, two may share the space), then timers, then a Shortcuts row of up to 3 user-chosen shortcuts beside it. The top row is always the thing that is live right now, never a static menu.
- **Per-app music source picker:** Settings → Music — the user chooses which apps may feed the music pill (PixelMusic by default). Apps not chosen — e.g. browser video — never appear in the island.
- **Curved sidebar (Arastoo reel — design pattern only, product unverified):** 56 dp icon rail → tap expands to 280 dp curved glass panel, asymmetric radii 28/8 dp, purple-black theme as option, badges, NOTICE card. Use as the design reference for the island's side panel / floating sidebar shape language. Do NOT cite "LUMEN" as a verified source — no such product was found.
- Companion circle for a second concurrent activity (ajitpal/SmartIsland): tappable circle beside the pill with a +1 badge, placeable left or right.
- Every setting shows its result instantly (live preview) — no blind toggles. 48 dp touch targets; respects reduced motion; TalkBack labels.
