### 5. SOUND EFFECTS — regenerate ALL of them, premium, distinct, fast, crisp (priority #2)
Build #4 regenerated all 13 WAVs and they still don't feel premium. The diagnosis (sourced — Android earcon guidance + Apple HIG + Material sound guidance): long decay/release tails (sound still ringing when the next tap starts, brain reads lag); slow attack / soft onset; overlapping releases stacking into a wash; bass-dependent tones lost on the Redmi speaker (nothing below 300 Hz survives); no transient layer (pure sine = "beep", not a physical click); all 13 too similar / too loud / too long — no hierarchy. **No published sound spec exists for MT Capsule, dynamicSpot, or ajitpal — do not invent one. The bar is iOS + Material/Android guidance below.**
- **ONE sonic family for all 13.** Layer A = click transient — 2–4 ms filtered-noise burst, high-pass 2 kHz, peak at t=0, gone by 5 ms. Layer B = main tone — sine fundamental + triangle 2nd harmonic at −12 dB (crystalline bell without harshness). Layer C (only where noted) = shimmer — sine one octave above the main tone, −18 dB, decaying in half the main tone's time. Register map: low 500–700 Hz = confirm/settle; mid 800–1,200 Hz = navigation; high 1,500–2,500 Hz = frequent micro-taps. Direction map: **rising = open/on/play/forward, falling = close/off/pause/back, two-note = state change, three-note = hero only.**
- **Format for every file:** mono WAV, 44.1 kHz, 16-bit, peak as listed, **no reverb tail baked in** (reverb is what made build #4 feel slow), **no silence at head or tail** — trim to the durations below, fade the last 5–10 ms to zero. Routine sounds −12 to −14 dBFS peak; hero −6 dB. Do NOT normalise all 13 to 0 dB. Randomisation = SoundPool `rate` (pitch) and `volume` jitter applied *at playback*, not baked into the WAV. Every sound is paired with a haptic tick fired from the **same call site** (sound + haptic must read as one event, within ~20–30 ms). If haptics are off, sound still plays alone — never make haptic the only channel.
- **The 13 recipes (implement exactly — duration / base freq / envelope attack-decay-release / loudness / jitter / haptic):**
  1. **Tap** — 45 ms; 1,600 Hz sine + click transient 2–4 kHz; sine + triangle 2nd harm. −12 dB; click 3 ms; 1/35/9 ms; **−12 dB**; rate 0.98–1.02, vol ±1 dB; `VIRTUAL_KEY` 10 ms light tick.
  2. **Expand** — 180 ms; sweep 600→1,200 Hz sine + shimmer 2,400 at −18 dB; click 3 ms at start; shimmer enters at 40 ms; 3/140/37 ms; **−9 dB**; rate 0.99–1.01, vol ±0.5 dB; `CONTEXT_CLICK` medium tick at start.
  3. **Collapse** — 150 ms; sweep 1,000→550 Hz sine + shimmer 2,000 at −18 dB (mirror of Expand, lower + shorter = finality); click 3 ms; 3/115/32 ms; **−10 dB**; rate 0.99–1.01, vol ±0.5 dB; `CONTEXT_CLICK`.
  4. **Music play** — 220 ms; 880→1,320 Hz (A5→E6, perfect 5th up), two notes 90 + 110 ms, 20 ms gap; sine + triangle harm.; no click (soft start); shimmer on 2nd note only; note envelopes 5/70/15 and 5/85/20 ms; **−8 dB**; rate 0.99–1.01, vol ±0.5 dB; `CONFIRM` light-then-strong ~30 ms.
  5. **Music pause** — 180 ms; 1,100→880 Hz (falling 3rd), two notes 80 + 80 ms, 20 ms gap; soft click 2 ms on note 1 only; 5/60/15 ms per note; **−10 dB**; rate 0.99–1.01, vol ±0.5 dB; `VIRTUAL_KEY`.
  6. **Music next** — 140 ms; 1,000→1,500 Hz fast rising blip + click transient; shimmer 3,000 at −18 dB, 40 ms; 2/105/33 ms; **−9 dB**; rate 0.97–1.03, vol ±1 dB; `KEYBOARD_TAP`.
  7. **Timer set** — 160 ms; 700 + 1,050 Hz (tick-chime), two notes 70 + 70 ms, 20 ms gap; click 2 ms; 3/120/37 ms total; **−10 dB**; rate 0.99–1.01, vol ±0.5 dB; `CLOCK_TICK`.
  8. **Timer done (HERO — only long sound)** — 650 ms; 880, 1,108, 1,318 Hz (A5–C#6–E6 major triad), three notes 150 + 180 + 260 ms, 30 ms gaps; shimmer octave-up on 3rd note only; no click; per note 5 ms attack, decay to 60% in 100 ms, release 40 ms; final release 60 ms; **−6 dB (loudest)**; rate 1.00 fixed (no pitch jitter — must be recognisable), vol ±0.5 dB; `CONFIRM` + second light tick at 300 ms.
  9. **Toggle ON** — 120 ms; 600→900 Hz rising single sweep; click 3 ms; 2/90/28 ms; **−10 dB**; rate 0.98–1.02, vol ±1 dB; `VIRTUAL_KEY`.
  10. **Toggle OFF** — 120 ms; 900→600 Hz falling single sweep (exact mirror of ON); click 3 ms; 2/90/28 ms; **−11 dB** (1 dB quieter = "less" than ON); rate 0.98–1.02, vol ±1 dB; `VIRTUAL_KEY`.
  11. **Vault add (save to Shelf)** — 260 ms; 520→780→1,040 Hz (C5–G5–C6), three notes 70 + 70 + 90 ms, 15 ms gaps; soft "lock" click 3 ms on note 1; shimmer on note 3; 3 ms attack each note; decay 50 ms; final release 45 ms; **−8 dB**; rate 0.99–1.01, vol ±0.5 dB; `LONG_PRESS` ~25 ms firmer tick.
  12. **Search open** — 170 ms; sweep 800→1,600 Hz sine + filtered-noise whoosh 3 kHz, −20 dB, 80 ms (whoosh under first 80 ms only); 3/130/37 ms; **−10 dB**; rate 0.99–1.01, vol ±0.5 dB; `CONTEXT_CLICK`.
  13. **Calc key (most frequent — quietest, shortest)** — 35 ms; 2,000 Hz sine + click transient 2 ms; **no** harmonic, **no** shimmer (keeps it boring on purpose — 200 presses/day must not fatigue); 1/26/8 ms; **−14 dB (quietest)**; rate 0.97–1.03, vol ±1 dB — widest jitter in the set; `KEYBOARD_TAP` 8 ms tick.
- **Distinctness rule:** no two events share the same (direction + note-count + register + duration). Tap (1,600 Hz, 45 ms) vs Calc (2,000 Hz, 35 ms) differ by register + loudness; ON vs OFF are exact mirrors; Expand vs Collapse are mirrors (180 vs 150 ms); Play vs Pause are opposite directions; Timer Set (2 notes, low) vs Timer Done (3 notes, triad, 650 ms) differ by note-count + duration + loudness.
- **What you must NOT do:** no main tone below 300 Hz; no file longer than its table duration; no baked-in reverb/delay tail; no normalising all files to 0 dB; no pure sine without a transient (except Timer Done and Music Play); no stereo widening; no silence at head/tail. Do NOT copy the unverified "iOS 150 Hz / 15 ms tap" claim from a social-media reel — 150 Hz is below this phone's speaker range.
- **SoundPool wiring:** preload all 13 at startup (first-play latency comes from loading, not the file); maxStreams 3–4, timer-done highest priority, calc/tap lowest; stop-before-replay for Tap/Calc (rapid taps must never stack into a wash); `play()` returning streamID 0 means a low-priority sound was refused — handle it, don't silently drop. UI sounds must not request audio focus — music in PixelMusic must continue undisturbed.
- **Verification (phone test, not "file exists in res/raw" — record the numbers in the test notes):** (A) Audibility at 50% volume, phone 30 cm away — every sound ≥2/3 ("clear"); none = 3 ("loud") except Timer Done; Calc Key 1–2 by design. (B) Blind distinctness — confusable set (Tap, Toggle ON, Toggle OFF, Expand, Music Play) ≥9/10 correct; full set ≥11/13. (C) Rapid-tap overlap — 10× fast calc taps = 10 clean ticks, no wash, no dropped sound. (D) Latency — sound perceived as simultaneous on 20/20 taps; slow-mo (240 fps) shows sound starting within ~4 frames (~17 ms) of contact, never more than ~100 ms. First-tap-only delay = preload bug, not a WAV bug. (E) Haptic sync — sound and haptic feel like one event; with haptics OFF the four test sounds are still identifiable by sound alone. (F) Fatigue — after 10 min normal use (20 calc keys, 10 toggles, 10 expand/collapse, 5 play/pause) Alex would keep sound ON. (G) No-interference — PixelMusic continues undisturbed. **Overall sound verdict: PASS only if A + B + C + D + E + G pass and F is "would keep sound ON".** If B fails, the recipes are wrong (not the phone). "Sounds good" without the Test A scores and Test B blind score is not a pass.
- Keep all 13 events distinct. Sounds stay in Settings → Motion with toggle + volume (default ON, 0.75). **Sound packs ("Glass"/"Pop"/"Soft") are DEFERRED to build #6** — do not build them now; the single-family regeneration above is the build-#5 sound work.

